<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><bns:Component xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bns="http://api.platform.boomi.com/" folderFullPath="Endeavour Management Services London Limited/edv.framework" componentId="8daf258f-72f7-4c33-9e24-6db5b6b0e1a2" version="14" name="Sub_TransactionLog_Consumer" type="process" createdDate="2026-09-14T11:18:25Z" modifiedDate="2026-11-04T08:08:45Z" deleted="false" currentVersion="true" folderName="edv.framework" folderId="Rjo4ODM3OTY0" branchName="main" branchId="Qjo1NDk1Njc"><bns:encryptedValues/><bns:description>UPDATED 2026-11-03: inserts run before close-outs inside a batch (Branch). For a close-out, an event younger than 15 minutes whose row is missing raises CLOSEOUT_ROW_NOT_FOUND and stays in the queue for retry; an older event is processed once without raising an error, so its message is acknowledged. | Event Streams consumer for the Endeavour Mining P2P framework, on topic "edv.transaction.log" (subscription "p2p-transaction-log-consumer"). RESILIENCE REDESIGN 2026-09-28: Sub_Generate_CorrelationId no longer writes to transaction_log directly (a brief SQL Server outage used to silently lose the row - Database V2 has no connection retry). Instead it publishes a LogPhase=START event here, same as the existing SUCCESS/ERROR close-out events. This process now branches on the event's logPhase (Route shape, shapeROUTE): START -&gt; INSERT the new row (Send_TransactionLog_Insert_V2, all 10 columns, same shape Sub_Generate_CorrelationId used to build directly); anything else (SUCCESS/ERROR) -&gt; the original UPDATE path (status/end_date/duration_ms computed server-side via Send_TransactionLog_UpdateStatus_V2). SQL Server (Database V2, EDV_INTEGRATION).
REBUILT AROUND CONSUME, NOT LISTEN (2026-09-14): the original design used Listen_P2P_ExecutionLog_Event as the Start shape. Confirmed via repeated deploy+trigger attempts that the subscription's "type" stays "NONE" - the target cloud runtime has no execution worker enabled, which Listen requires to attach (Produce on the same connection works fine, isolating the gap to Listen specifically - see platform_entities/event_streams.md). Since enabling that worker is a cloud-runtime administration action outside this skill's reach, the Start shape now uses Consume_P2P_ExecutionLog_Event instead (same topic/subscription - Consume can read a subscription regardless of which operation type created it). Consume is an ordinary on-demand execution needing no worker; the tradeoff is this process must be triggered externally (scheduling, same gap/pattern as Scheduled_Purge_Retention - no CLI/API tool in this skill configures a schedule, set via Atom Management -&gt; Scheduling or the ProcessSchedules API) rather than reacting to messages the instant they arrive. Consume's maxMessages=10 means each scheduled run can process a small batch, not just one message - every downstream shape already operates per-document (confirmed throughout this framework), so the existing Notify/DDP-extraction/Try-Catch/Map/Send chain needed no structural change to handle multiple documents per execution; Try/Catch continues to isolate per-message failures (confirmed in try_catch_step.md: document-level, not batch-level). acknowledgeLater=true on the Consume operation means a message that fails processing returns to the backlog for automatic redelivery rather than being lost - safe here since the downstream action is an idempotent UPDATE keyed on transaction_id. Process-level allowSimultaneous flipped true-&gt;false and updateRunDates flipped false-&gt;true to match a scheduled-batch process instead of a continuous listener (see process_component.md's start-step-type guidance).
Previously used a guessed SP_UPSERT_TRANSACTION_LOG signature against a placeholder SQL Server connection and a full upsert-of-everything design; corrected once the real schema was confirmed (transaction_id is a synchronously-generated UUID FK target, not something this process needs to create). MIGRATED 2026-09-25 from MySQL/Database (Legacy) to SQL Server/Database V2: a Message step builds the update request JSON directly from the inbound event's profile elements (no Map component - V2 profiles are JSON, driven by named $param placeholders). All logic remains native (Message + Database V2 connector), no scripting. CorrelationId is extracted as a DDP before the Try/Catch so it is available on both the success and error Notify paths. | built with boomi-companion v1.0.57</bns:description><bns:object><process xmlns="" allowSimultaneous="false" enableUserLog="false" processLogOnErrorOnly="false" purgeDataImmediately="false" stopProcessingIfZeroDocuments="true" updateRunDates="true" workload="general"><shapes><shape image="start" name="shape1" shapetype="start" userlabel="Consume" x="48.0" y="46.0"><configuration><connectoraction actionType="Consume" allowDynamicCredentials="NONE" connectionId="54d36e66-c760-45a9-91b2-aa28f83a43d2" connectorType="officialboomi-X3979C-events-prod" hideSettings="false" operationId="b2470abe-2d06-47c2-a7e7-289e85d7e6c2"><parameters/><dynamicProperties/></connectoraction></configuration><dragpoints><dragpoint name="shape1.dragpoint1" toShape="shape2" x="240.0" y="56.0"/></dragpoints><stepnotes><note title="">&lt;p&gt;up to 10 messages per poll (was Listen - see description)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</note></stepnotes></shape><shape image="notify_icon" name="shape2" shapetype="notify" userlabel="Log raw inbound" x="256.0" y="48.0"><configuration><notify disableEvent="true" enableUserLog="false" perExecution="false" title=""><notifyMessage>[Sub_TransactionLog_Consumer inbound event] {1}</notifyMessage><notifyMessageLevel>INFO</notifyMessageLevel><n